I am also a newbie when it comes to Apps Script, however I am volunteering my time to help out my kids' Playcentre (in New Zealand this is a non-profit parent-led preschool) by creating a handy Google Form we can use, that generates a preformatted Google Doc.  I have followed and entered your script and added the one, someone in these comments mentioned, about embedding an image from a URL collected by the 'File Upload' option in Forms. The form I am working on though, allows multiple images to be uploaded. But as you probably know, the URLs of the multiple images get added into a single cell, separated by comma and space. At the moment - if I upload multiple images to my form, only one gets embedded in the generated doc. Do you have a handy tips/script on how to embed all the photos I've uploaded in the Google Doc?
Below is what I'm using for it (basically copy/paste from these comments).
Many thanks in advance!
Bilyana

//function embedding image to document with a specified size
    var replaceTextToImage = function(body, searchText, fileId) {
    var width = 200; // Please set this.
    var blob = DriveApp.getFileById(fileId).getBlob();
    var r = body.findText(searchText).getElement();
    r.asText().setText("");
    var img = r.getParent().asParagraph().insertInlineImage(0, blob);
    var w = img.getWidth();
    var h = img.getHeight();

    img.setWidth(width);
    img.setHeight(width * h / w);
  }

  // Get the image fileID
  var image = e.values[xx]// xx being the row number in which the link to the uploaded image is
  var imageID = String(image).split("=")[1]; //gives you the fileID of the uploaded image

    // Use the function replaceTextToImage
  replaceTextToImage(body, '{{Photos}}', imageID); // replaces the {{image}} tag with the uploaded image

